KZ3 patch 2098 (RSX pass 93): mouse hover and click in the game's GUM menus (the RE notes "Pass 93").
ENHANCEMENT. libs/input/pad_menu_mouse.h (new, pure; host test tools/smoke/test_menu_mouse.sh): kz3_menu_hit_test
(RE pass 143's spec), PadMenuInject (a click or wheel notch = one delivered pad packet pressed, one released),
PadMenuHover (hover only after a pointer move, never while the pad is used), pmm_event_bits. libs/input/pad_mouse.h/.c:
g_mouse_guest {x, y, valid, seq} (the one pointer position, guest pixels via rsx_display_client_to_guest at
WM_MOUSEMOVE), clicks/wheel queued while a menu is up, pad_cursor_decide's new `menu` input (no hide, no clip),
KZ3_MENU_MOUSE_SCRIPT test events posted as window messages. libs/input/cellPad.c: port-0 hooks g_pad_menu_bits_hook
(adds the presses; gets the pad's own menu buttons) and g_pad_menu_sent_hook (packet delivered), mouse-bound keys
off while a menu is up, pad_kb_capture_busy. libs/video/rsx_null_backend.c: hands rsx_display_client_to_guest to
pad_mouse.c. The guest side (GUM context capture, tag walk, SetFocus) is port/kz3/main.cpp kz3_menu_mouse_*.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): menu-mouse sent hook at upstream's emit (freshness now finalized earlier upstream, 6eb26c1e).

